---
/**
 * /quoted/ — the work that carries its own price, in one place.
 *
 * WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS. Six things this practice sells are quoted in writing
 * before they start, and until now every one of them appeared in exactly ONE
 * place: the capability block on the three comparison sheets. A visitor who
 * never opened a comparison document could not learn that a small online store
 * is buyable here at all. They are not refusals and they are not free — they are
 * real work with a real price, and they had no door.
 *
 * IT PUBLISHES NO FIGURE, and that is what keeps D94 intact. That rule says
 * /services/ stops at five figures and any further product publishes on its own
 * page, because a price list becomes a menu once the prices stack. Nothing here
 * carries a number, so this page is a door rather than a sixth panel on a price
 * list.
 *
 * THE SIX SHARED ITEMS ONLY, AND THE OMISSION IS DELIBERATE. The store
 * configurator lives in EXTRA under `stores` in src/lib/capabilities.js, which
 * is sheet-specific by design, and scripts/lib/capability-check.mjs asserts in
 * BOTH directions that a sheet's own items are ABSENT from its sisters. Pulling
 * the stores-only item onto a general page would not break that check — it does
 * not read this page — but it would break what the check MEANS, which is that
 * sheet-specific copy stays on its sheet. The page links to /stores/ for it
 * instead, which is where it is already argued properly.
 *
 * EVERY SENTENCE COMES FROM src/lib/capabilities.js AND NONE IS WRITTEN HERE.
 * That module's own header names the reason: §3 of the signed website Scope is
 * the source under all of it, and a second copy written in a sales voice drifts
 * the moment one of them is softened in a copy pass. A client then signs one
 * thing having read another.
 */
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { SCOPED, HEADINGS, INTROS, assertCapabilities } from '../lib/capabilities.js';
import { ArrowUpRight, FileText } from '@lucide/astro';

assertCapabilities('quoted.astro');

const origin = new URL(Astro.site!).origin;

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': `${origin}/quoted/#page`,
    name: 'Work I quote before it starts',
    description:
      'Six things this practice builds that are priced on their own, in writing, before any of them begins — rather than folded into a build price.',
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${origin}/#website` },
  },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Work I quote before it starts"
  description="Six things I build that carry their own price, agreed in writing before anything begins. Not extras, not refusals — separate work, named up front."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
    <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-16 pb-10 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-14">
      <p class="mono-label">Real work · its own price · agreed before it starts</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        {HEADINGS.scoped}.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        {INTROS.scoped}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        None of this is an extra tacked onto an invoice later. Each one is named, priced and agreed
        before it begins, and you decide whether it happens at all. If you never ask for any of it,
        a build costs exactly what the build costs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-14 sm:py-20">
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-5">
      {
        SCOPED.map((item) => (
          <li class="panel flex flex-col gap-3 p-7">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <FileText class="mt-1 size-5 shrink-0 text-accent" />
              <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">{item.what}</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{item.detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    {/* THE STORE CONFIGURATOR IS NAMED AND NOT REPEATED. See the header: it is
        stores-only copy in the capability module, and the argument for it lives
        on the page that can make it properly. A link is honest; a second copy
        of the sentence is the drift this whole module exists to prevent. */}
    <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      One more sits with the work it belongs to. If you sell something a customer has to configure
      before buying — a size, a finish, a cut to length — that builder is quoted work too, and the
      quote covers keeping it working when your platform changes.{' '}
      <a class="link-sweep" href="/stores/">It is argued on the selling-online comparison →</a>
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact/?intent=quote">
        Ask what yours would cost <ArrowUpRight class="size-4" />
      </a>
      <a class="link-sweep text-sm" href="/services/">Or start with what a build includes →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
